{"actions":[{"date":"2026-07-15","source":"Senate","text":"Received in the Senate and Read twice and referred to the Committee on Banking, Housing, and Urban Affairs.","type":"IntroReferral"},{"date":"2026-07-14","source":"House floor actions","text":"Motion to reconsider laid on the table Agreed to without objection.","type":"Floor"},{"date":"2026-07-14","source":"House floor actions","text":"On passage Passed by the Yeas and Nays: 221 - 201 (Roll no. 240). (text: CR H4441-4442)","type":"Floor"},{"date":"2026-07-14","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Passed/agreed to in House: On passage Passed by the Yeas and Nays: 221 - 201 (Roll no. 240).","type":"Floor"},{"date":"2026-07-14","source":"House floor actions","text":"On motion to recommit Failed by the Yeas and Nays: 208 - 217 (Roll no. 239).","type":"Floor"},{"date":"2026-07-14","source":"House floor actions","text":"Considered as unfinished business. (consideration: CR H4451-4452)","type":"Floor"},{"date":"2026-07-14","source":"House floor actions","text":"POSTPONED PROCEEDINGS - At the conclusion of debate on H.R. 1181 the Chair put the question on the motion to recommit and by voice vote, announced the noes had prevailed. Mr. Frost demanded the yeas and nays and the Chair postponed further proceedings until a time to be announced.","type":"Floor"},{"date":"2026-07-14","source":"House floor actions","text":"The previous question on the motion to recommit was ordered pursuant to clause 2(b) of rule XIX.","type":"Floor"},{"date":"2026-07-14","source":"House floor actions","text":"Mr. Frost moved to recommit to the Committee on Financial Services. (CR H4445)","type":"Floor"},{"date":"2026-07-14","source":"House floor actions","text":"The previous question was ordered pursuant to the rule.","type":"Floor"},{"date":"2026-07-14","source":"House floor actions","text":"DEBATE - The House proceeded with one hour of debate on H.R. 1181.","type":"Floor"},{"date":"2026-07-14","source":"House floor actions","text":"Rule provides for consideration of H.R. 139, H.R. 8595, H.R. 9237 and H.R. 1181. The resolution provides for consideration of H.R. 139, H.R. 9237, and H.R. 1181 under a closed rule, and H.R. 8595 under a structured rule with one hour of debate and one motion to reconsider on each bill.","type":"Floor"},{"date":"2026-07-14","source":"House floor actions","text":"Considered under the provisions of rule H. Res. 1423. (consideration: CR H4441-4445)","type":"Floor"},{"date":"2026-07-14","source":"House floor actions","text":"Rule H. Res. 1423 passed House.","type":"Floor"},{"date":"2026-07-13","source":"House floor actions","text":"Rules Committee Resolution H. Res. 1423 Reported to House. Rule provides for consideration of H.R. 139, H.R. 8595, H.R. 9237 and H.R. 1181. The resolution provides for consideration of H.R. 139, H.R. 9237, and H.R. 1181 under a closed rule, and H.R. 8595 under a structured rule with one hour of debate and one motion to reconsider on each bill.","type":"Floor"},{"date":"2026-06-23","source":"House floor actions","text":"Rules Committee Resolution H. Res. 1377 Reported to House. Rule provides for consideration of H.R. 1181, H.R. 9022, H.R. 8595 and H.R. 9237. The resolution provides for consideration of H.R. 1181 and H.R. 9237 under a closed rule and H.R. 9022 and H.R. 8595 under a structured rule. The resolution provides for one hour of general debate and one motion to recommit on each bill.","type":"Floor"},{"date":"2026-02-25","source":"House floor actions","text":"Placed on the Union Calendar, Calendar No. 447.","type":"Calendars"},{"date":"2026-02-25","source":"House floor actions","text":"Reported (Amended) by the Committee on Financial Services. H. Rept. 119-522.","type":"Committee"},{"date":"2026-02-25","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Reported (Amended) by the Committee on Financial Services. H. Rept. 119-522.","type":"Committee"},{"date":"2025-12-17","source":"House committee actions","text":"Ordered to be Reported (Amended) by the Yeas and Nays: 29 - 23.","type":"Committee"},{"date":"2025-12-17","source":"House committee actions","text":"Committee Consideration and Mark-up Session Held","type":"Committee"},{"date":"2025-12-16","source":"House committee actions","text":"Committee Consideration and Mark-up Session Held","type":"Committee"},{"date":"2025-02-11","source":"House floor actions","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Financial Services.","type":"IntroReferral"},{"date":"2025-02-11","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Introduced in House","type":"IntroReferral"},{"date":"2025-02-11","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Introduced in House","type":"IntroReferral"}],"amendments":{"items":[{"action":"On agreeing to the Rules amendment (A001) Agreed to without objection.","amends":null,"chamber":"House of Representatives","date":"2026-07-14","id":"hamdt-230","label":"H.Amdt. 230","purpose":"Pursuant to the provisions of H.Res. 1423, the amendment in the nature of a substitute recommended by the Committee on Financial Services is considered adopted.","sponsor":{"bioguide_id":null,"name":null,"party":null,"state":null},"status":"Agreed to","submitted":"2026-07-14","url":"https://www.congress.gov/amendment/119th-congress/house-amendment/230"}],"total":1},"analysis_status":"scored","bipartisan_band":null,"chamber":"House","committees":[{"activities":[{"date":"2026-07-15","name":"Referred To"}],"chamber":"Senate","code":"ssbk00","name":"Banking, Housing, and Urban Affairs Committee","subcommittees":[]},{"activities":[{"date":"2026-07-14","name":"Unknown"},{"date":"2026-07-14","name":"Unknown"},{"date":"2026-02-25","name":"Reported By"},{"date":"2025-12-17","name":"Markup By"},{"date":"2025-12-16","name":"Markup By"},{"date":"2025-02-11","name":"Referred To"}],"chamber":"House","code":"hsba00","name":"Financial Services Committee","subcommittees":[]}],"cosponsor_count":132,"fetched_at":"2026-10-26T21:28:42+00:00","history":[{"day":"2026-10-26","importance":50,"viability":72.6}],"id":"119-hr-1181","importance":50,"importance_band":"moderate","importance_detail":{"consistent":true,"dimension_mean":50.0,"dimensions":[{"assessment":"Affects all payment card networks, financial processing entities, and firearms retailers across the United States.","evidence":"A payment card network may not require-- (A) a firearms retailer to use a merchant category code","evidence_verified":true,"key":"population","score":60},{"assessment":"Requires financial institutions and card networks to alter merchant coding practices and subjects violators to enforcement actions by the Attorney General.","evidence":"The Attorney General shall enforce this section... and bring an action in Federal court to enjoin the violating behavior","evidence_verified":false,"key":"magnitude","score":50},{"assessment":"Does not state specific federal appropriations or budgetary expenditures, relying on existing Department of Justice enforcement mechanisms.","evidence":null,"evidence_verified":false,"key":"fiscal","score":20},{"assessment":"Imposes federal prohibitions on commercial payment coding systems and expressly preempts all state and local laws regulating these specific merchant category codes.","evidence":"Any law of a State or local government regulating the assignment, use, or disclosure of merchant category codes... is hereby preempted","evidence_verified":false,"key":"scope","score":60},{"assessment":"Establishes permanent prohibitions on payment card coding practices alongside ongoing annual reporting requirements by the Attorney General.","evidence":"The Attorney General shall, each year, submit a report to the Congress","evidence_verified":true,"key":"duration","score":60}],"missing_information":["Estimates of administrative and compliance costs for payment networks and covered entities."],"rationale":"This bill prohibits payment card networks and covered entities from requiring or using specific merchant category codes that distinguish firearms retailers from general-merchandise or sporting-goods retailers.","score":50},"importance_meta":{"generated_at":"2026-10-26T21:32:04+00:00","model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","source_basis":"text+summary","source_urls":["https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr1181/BILLS-119hr1181rfs.htm"]},"introduced_date":"2025-02-11","is_demo":false,"label":"H.R. 1181","latest_action":{"date":"2026-07-15","text":"Received in the Senate and Read twice and referred to the Committee on Banking, Housing, and Urban Affairs."},"members":[{"chamber":"House","district":"2","id":"M001235","name":"Rep. Moore, Riley","party":"R","role":"sponsor","state":"WV"},{"chamber":"House","date":"2025-02-11","district":"6","id":"B001282","name":"Rep. Barr, Andy","original":true,"party":"R","role":"cosponsor","state":"KY"},{"chamber":"House","date":"2025-02-11","district":"9","id":"H001067","name":"Rep. Hudson, Richard","original":true,"party":"R","role":"cosponsor","state":"NC"},{"chamber":"House","date":"2025-02-11","district":"4","id":"B001314","name":"Rep. Bean, Aaron","original":true,"party":"R","role":"cosponsor","state":"FL"},{"chamber":"House","date":"2025-02-11","district":"6","id":"C001118","name":"Rep. Cline, Ben","original":true,"party":"R","role":"cosponsor","state":"VA"},{"chamber":"House","date":"2025-02-11","district":"10","id":"P000605","name":"Rep. Perry, Scott","original":true,"party":"R","role":"cosponsor","state":"PA"},{"chamber":"House","date":"2025-02-11","district":"24","id":"V000134","name":"Rep. Van Duyne, Beth","original":true,"party":"R","role":"cosponsor","state":"TX"},{"chamber":"House","date":"2025-02-11","district":"2","id":"G000558","name":"Rep. Guthrie, Brett","original":true,"party":"R","role":"cosponsor","state":"KY"},{"chamber":"House","date":"2025-02-11","district":"10","id":"C001129","name":"Rep. Collins, Mike","original":true,"party":"R","role":"cosponsor","state":"GA"},{"chamber":"House","date":"2025-02-11","district":"1","id":"F000475","name":"Rep. Finstad, Brad","original":true,"party":"R","role"